.TH NETMAILER 8N UniSoft
.SH NAME
netmailer \- deliver mail to 
.SM BNET
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/netmailer
.I from-address
.I to-host
.I to-user
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Netmailer\^
queues the letter found on its standard input
for delivery to the host and user specified.
The actual delivery will be performed by the
.SM BNET
mailer daemon 
.RB ( /etc/bnetmaild ).
.PP
If the letter does not appear to have a full
.SM BNET
header,
.I netmailer\^
will insert "Date:" and "From:"
fields in the proper format.
The "From:" person
is determined by the 
.I from-address\^
argument,
with colons translated to periods
and "@<local-host>" appended.
The "<local-host>" is obtained from the file 
.BR /usr/lib/uucp/\s-1SYSTEMNAME\s+1 .
.SH FILES
/usr/spool/netmail/\(**
.SH SEE ALSO
delivermail(8N), netmail(8N).
.\"	 @(#)netmailer.8n	 5.2 of 7/26/84
